## Summary

The 3MF exporter and importer load `adm-zip` with `require('adm-zip')`, but `package.json` lists it only under `devDependencies`. A consumer that installs the production dependencies (`xmldom` only) gets `Cannot find module 'adm-zip'` as soon as it saves or opens a 3MF file.

## Environment

- Revision `66cb26df3b031f0bf6976d4e88dc89721983afa4` (default branch `master`)
- Node.js v22.23.3 and npm 10.9.9 (Docker image `node:22-slim`, Linux)
- `npm install` and `npm run build` complete without errors; verified on 2026-10-16

## Steps to reproduce

```sh
npm install
npm run build
node repro.js   # repro.js holds the script below, saved in the repository root
```

Then run the script in a directory that has only what a consumer installs (the production dependencies):

```sh
mkdir ../consumer && cp -r package.json dist repro.js ../consumer && cd ../consumer
npm install --omit=dev
node repro.js
```

```js
const fs = require('fs');
const { Scene } = require('./dist/aspose/threed');
const { Mesh } = require('./dist/aspose/threed/entities');
const { Vector4 } = require('./dist/aspose/threed/utilities');

function triangle() {
  const mesh = new Mesh('tri');
  mesh.controlPoints = [new Vector4(10, 20, 30, 1), new Vector4(11, 20, 30, 1), new Vector4(10, 21, 30, 1)];
  mesh.createPolygon(0, 1, 2);
  return mesh;
}

const scene = new Scene();
scene.rootNode.createChildNode('n', triangle());
try { scene.save('t.3mf'); } catch (e) { console.log(e.constructor.name + ': ' + e.message.split('\n')[0]); }
```

## Expected

`adm-zip` is installed together with the library (listed under `dependencies`) and `t.3mf` is written.

## Actual result

```
Error: Cannot find module 'adm-zip'
```

## Where in the repository

- `package.json:26,31` (`@types/adm-zip` and `adm-zip` under `devDependencies`; `dependencies` holds only `xmldom`)
- `src/aspose/threed/formats/threemf/ThreeMfExporter.ts:162` and `src/aspose/threed/formats/threemf/ThreeMfImporter.ts:53`

